Wedding Day Overview
This timeline outlines a smooth flow for a 4:00 PM ceremony on Saturday, June 15, 2025. The schedule prioritizes a relaxed pace by incorporating buffer periods for guest movement and photography, ensuring key moments like the First Look and Grand Entrance occur without rushing.

Timeline Logistics & Venue Context
This schedule assumes that the ceremony and reception take place at the same venue or within a 5-10 minute drive of each other. A 30-minute duration is allocated for the ceremony, which is standard for non-religious or semi-religious civil unions. Sunset on June 15 is typically late (around 8:30 PM), allowing for potential "golden hour" photos during dinner service if desired.

Detailed Day-of Schedule
Time | Event | Details & Buffer Notes
2:00 PM | First Look | Private moment for the couple; allows for early photos
2:30 PM | Formal Photos | Wedding party and immediate family portraits; wrap by 3:30 PM
3:30 PM | Guest Arrival Buffer | Couple in hiding; guests arrive and take seats
4:00 PM | Wedding Ceremony | Processional begins; exchange of vows and rings
4:30 PM | Recessional & Transition | 15-minute buffer for family exit and guest movement
4:45 PM | Cocktail Hour | Guests mingle; extended family photos if needed
5:45 PM | Reception Transition | Guests move to dining area; 15-minute seating buffer
6:00 PM | Grand Entrance | Introduction of wedding party and newlyweds
6:15 PM | Dinner Service | Plated or buffet service begins immediately after entrance
7:15 PM | Toasts & Speeches | Scheduled toward the end of the meal as plates are cleared
7:45 PM | First Dance | Couple opens the dance floor; transition to party music

